  "description": "About STARFORGE: 24-Hour National Level Hackathon Welcome to STARFORGE , an intensive, high-octane 24-hour space related hackathon designed to push the boundaries of technical innovation, engineering, and problem-solving. Whether you are a software architect or a hardware enthusiast, STARFORGE provides the ultimate launchpad to forge your ideas into reality. The hackathon features challenges split across two tracks: Software Track Hardware Track Problem Statements will be released soon... Important Guidelines & Team Structure Team Composition: 3-4 members per team . Gender Diversity (Mandatory): Every team must include at least 1 female member to be eligible for participation. Free Registration Stages Stage 1: Online Screening & Pitch Submission Teams must submit an initial abstract and pitch presentation (PPT) adhering strictly to the official deck template. The technical committee will screen entries to select the final teams for the offline hackathon. Stage 2: The Main 24-Hour Offline Hackathon Location: BMS Institute of technology and Management The Build: A grueling 24-hour hacking window filled with intense development, mentoring, and mini-games. Final Evaluation: Projects will be judged live by a panel of industry experts through interactive demos. Rewards and Prizes Compete for glory and a slice of the ₹65,000 cash prize pool : Overall Winner: ₹25,000 ️ Hardware Track Winner: ₹15,000 Software Track Winner: ₹15,000 Best Innovation: ₹10,000 Beside cash prizes, attendees stand a chance to win exclusive space-themed merchandise, certification, and valuable sponsor learning credits.",
